The root cause of the bug is that the implementation allowed the collapse of transparent huge pages (THP) for files opened in read-only mode and mapped with the execute flag, without restricting file types. This included non-regular files like block devices, which can lead to unexpected behaviors and bugs when THP is applied to them, as they are not meant to support such memory optimizations. By not properly checking whether a file is a regular file, the system could inadvertently compromise its memory management stability and security.

