```c
if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_READ_ONLY_THP_FOR_FS) && vma->vm_file &&
    (vm_flags & VM_EXEC)) {
```
Reason:
This code allows the collapse of transparent huge pages (THP) for any file that is opened in read-only mode and has the execute flag set, without checking if the file is a regular file. This oversight permits non-regular files, such as block devices, to have THP applied, which can lead to unexpected behaviors and bugs.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
return !inode_is_open_for_write(inode) &&
    S_ISREG(inode->i_mode);
```
Reason:
This code adds a check to ensure that the file is a regular file (using `S_ISREG`) before allowing THP collapse. By restricting the operation to only regular files, the patch mitigates the risk of applying THP to inappropriate file types, thus enhancing memory management stability and security.


